                  <msItem>
                     <title>Missale, etc.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">A very pretty book. Small folios, 24 long
                        lines. At end, fol. 128r, is a form added s. xiv, with rubric -- erased but
                        legible -- "In die an[n]iuersar' fundatorum Kenelworth". In the litanies --
                        original -- Augustine and Peter are doubled.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Medieval binding of bare wooden boards.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="12XX">s. xiii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_277">Kenilworth, Warwickshire.
                        Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin. </orgName><p>The form of monastic
                        profession, fol. iii recto, is "Ego frater .N. offerens trado me ipsum
                        diuine pietati in ecclesia sancte marie de Kenilleworth serviturum secundum
                        Regulam sancti Augustini...".</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">"Liber Roberti Baskett de Blandford Bryan
                     Dorset" (s. xviii).</provenance>
               </history>
